1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,910
This course shows you how to use the AI agent to do your data engineering. You tell it what you want, and you review what it builds. This video sets it up: turn on AI agents, choose what your agent may do, and open it.

2
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:18,271
First, an administrator turns on AI agents.

3
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:23,441
Under Admin, open System, then AI agents.

4
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,293
Turn on Enabled.

5
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:43,642
The provider can be Anthropic, OpenAI, or Other, for any OpenAI-compatible service. This course uses Anthropic: its endpoint URL and model are already filled in.

6
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:53,024
The model here is the one each conversation starts with. Type its name as the provider gives it. This course uses claude-haiku-5-5.

7
00:00:54,040 --> 00:01:03,054
The context window is the most the model reads at once. Leave it as it is: on Save, it is set to what the provider says the model holds.

8
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:08,875
Paste in the API key. It is stored encrypted, and never shown again.

9
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:16,430
Kept for sets how long a conversation lasts: one nobody adds to for ninety days is deleted.

10
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:24,590
Save. Saving asks the endpoint for a short answer, to check the key works. The key now shows as Stored.

11
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:31,401
Now set what your own agent may do. Open the menu under your name, then Agent permissions.

12
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:50,264
Your agent never holds more than you do. An area is the shared configuration, or one worker group. In each area, your agent holds the lower of your level and the one you give it here.

13
00:01:51,200 --> 00:02:01,750
A viewer is read-only. An editor can read and write, on a branch. A deployer has the final approval over changes, before they go live.

14
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:07,416
Choose editor, so the agent can build, and you still decide what deploys.

15
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:09,767
Save.

16
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:17,034
The Agent button opens your agent at the bottom of any page.

17
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:26,011
You type here. What your agent does appears above, as it happens.

18
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:41,909
The model chip beside the prompt shows Haiku 5.5. Open it to pick another model your key reaches, or how much effort the model puts in.

19
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,890
Check on learning.

20
00:02:51,090 --> 00:02:57,150
Your agent is set to deployer, but you are an editor. Can it deploy?

21
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:05,200
No. It never holds more than you do.

22
00:03:06,100 --> 00:03:09,100
Where do you turn AI agents on?

23
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:17,704
Admin, System, AI agents.

24
00:03:18,604 --> 00:03:23,070
Next, you have the agent build a pipeline from live data.
